#[doc = "Replaces the disk image at the given index with a new disk.\n\nReplaces the disk image associated with index.\nArguments to pass in info have same requirements as retro_load_game().\nVirtual disk tray must be ejected when calling this.\n\nPassing `NULL` to this function indicates\nthat the frontend has removed this disk image from its internal list.\nAs a result, calls to this function can change the number of available disk indexes.\n\nFor example, calling <tt>replace_image_index(1, NULL)</tt>\nwill remove the disk image at index 1,\nand the disk image at index 2 (if any)\nwill be moved to the newly-available index 1.\n\n# Arguments\n\n* `index` - The index of the disk image to replace.\n* `info` - Details about the new disk image,\nor `NULL` if the disk image at the given index should be discarded.\nThe semantics of each field are the same as in `retro_load_game.`\n\n# Returns\n\n* `true` if the disk image was successfully replaced\nor removed from the playlist,\n`false` if the tray is not ejected\nor if there was an error.\n"]
